{%- comment -%}
  Product card — "Available in 18K, 22K".

  The design's karat note, and the karat sentence only. Size stays out, as it
  always has: listing every option instead put the ring sizes on the card —
  "18K / Test 21K · Test Size 6.5 / Test Size 5.5" — which the design never
  shows.

  **Every value the option carries is listed, whatever the stock.** An option
  value exists because the piece can be made that way, so a sold-out karat is
  still a karat the shop offers; filtering on `available` would make the
  sentence flicker as inventory moved.

  **Sorted smallest karat first, numerically.** A plain string sort puts "22K"
  before "9K", so the number is pulled out of each value and zero-padded into a
  sortable key which is then thrown away. A value with no number in it sorts to
  the front rather than vanishing.

  The option is matched on its name — "purity" or "karat" — and not nominated,
  for the same reason `card-option.liquid` derives its own: a block cannot
  share a setting with its siblings, so anything a merchant could set here
  would be one more thing to keep in step by hand.

  It renders nothing where the piece has no such option, which is most of a
  catalogue that is not this one.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product

  assign karat_option = blank
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign option_down = option.name | downcase
    if option_down contains 'purity' or option_down contains 'karat'
      assign karat_option = option
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign options_note = ''
  if karat_option != blank
    assign karat_keys = ''
    for value in karat_option.values
      assign digits = value | downcase | remove: 'karat' | remove: 'kt' | remove: 'k' | strip
      assign number = digits | plus: 0
      assign pad = ''
      if number < 10
        assign pad = '00'
      elsif number < 100
        assign pad = '0'
      endif
      assign karat_keys = karat_keys | append: pad | append: number | append: '~' | append: value | append: '||'
    endfor

    assign karat_keys = karat_keys | split: '||' | sort
    assign karat_list = ''
    for key in karat_keys
      assign label = key | split: '~' | last
      if karat_list == blank
        assign karat_list = label
      else
        assign karat_list = karat_list | append: ', ' | append: label
      endif
    endfor

    if karat_list != blank
      assign options_note = 'products.available_in' | t: list: karat_list
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if options_note != blank -%}
  <div class="card__note" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ options_note }}</div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.product_card_available.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.product_card_available.name"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
